attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on the sulfonate genes.** Column 0, `ssuA`, is a spine, carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, 0.13 bits {S1}.

@variable **Columns 1 to 3, `ssuD` to `ssuB`, are variable**, carried by 89 to 90%, [[aliphatic sulfonate transport]] {S2, Q}. The spine at columns 12 to 19, `mukB` to `ycaR`, is named 57 to 99.8%, fewest at column 14, `mukF`, 57% {S7}. Columns 33 to 79 are fork and variable, carried by 49 to 90%, in a region of plasticity in 11 to 25% of calls {S16}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 95 against 90%, and hesitates less there, 0.08 against 0.43 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 65, `poxB`, is a variable column, at 0.77 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on the putrescine genes.** Column 79, `potI`, is a fork, carried by 57% of chromosomes {S16.c79, E}. A second family there, `potH`, is carried by 30% {S16.c79}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.32 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.71 against 0.14 bits, and names fewer genes, 65% against 95% {C}.

